उत्सर्ग m. pouring forth, emission, excretion;
 laying
aside, taking off, loosening, delivering, abandoning, giving up,
closing, completion (esp. of the study of the Veda);
 oblation, present.

उत्सादन n. putting off, interrupting, injuring,
destroying;
 rubbing or chafing the limbs.

उत्सिक्त a. exuberant, abundant in, swelled by (instr or
—˚);
 overstrained (lit. & fig.);
 extravagant, haughty, disordered
(mind).

उत्सुक a. restless, uneasy, intent;
 regretful, sad, anxious
about, longing or wishing for (loc., प्रति, or —˚);
 *caring about
(loc. or instr.). Abstr. ˚ता f.

उत्सेक m. overflow, excess;
 extravagance, haughtiness;
poss. ˚किन्.
